00:08:47.969 --> 00:08:50.009
It's across your whole life.

00:08:50.009 --> 00:08:51.996
A lot of young people
have that mindset of,

00:08:51.996 --> 00:08:55.109
"Oh, I don't even wanna
live 'till I'm 40 or 70.

00:08:55.109 --> 00:08:56.819
I'd rather get all my fun in now."

00:08:56.819 --> 00:08:59.969
And you only say that up
until you're 30, or 40, or 50,

00:08:59.969 --> 00:09:00.809
and then you realized

00:09:00.809 --> 00:09:02.369
how much more you want to keep living life

00:09:02.369 --> 00:09:03.539
and enjoying the different

00:09:03.539 --> 00:09:04.670
stages of your life.
(keyboard clacks)

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:07.289
- I am Sydney, I am 29 years old,

00:09:07.289 --> 00:09:09.029
and I am making my neck long.

00:09:09.029 --> 00:09:11.879
- What this thing does is
not make your neck long.

00:09:11.879 --> 00:09:14.399
It can make the appearance
of your neck long

00:09:14.399 --> 00:09:16.799
by pushing down the clavicles,

00:09:16.799 --> 00:09:18.749
which are your collarbones here,

00:09:18.749 --> 00:09:21.719
and literally changing the
angle of your top ribs.

00:09:21.719 --> 00:09:23.519
So it looks like your neck is longer

00:09:23.519 --> 00:09:25.319
but it's actually not becoming longer.

00:09:25.319 --> 00:09:26.339
- [Sydney] Because of the necklace,

00:09:26.339 --> 00:09:29.129
I had to change everything in my life.

00:09:29.129 --> 00:09:30.359
Even the way I eat.

00:09:30.359 --> 00:09:32.009
I can feel my throat

00:09:32.009 --> 00:09:36.029
pressing against the back of
the necklace when I swallow.

00:09:36.029 --> 00:09:38.039
- If you're limiting your range of motion,

00:09:38.039 --> 00:09:40.229
you're actually creating restrictions

00:09:40.229 --> 00:09:42.059
and blood flow weaknesses

00:09:42.059 --> 00:09:44.099
in the stabilizing muscles of the neck.

00:09:44.099 --> 00:09:45.929
And as a result, they're
setting yourself up

00:09:45.929 --> 00:09:47.609
for future tension headache,
(text pops)

00:09:47.609 --> 00:09:48.839
compression headaches,
(text pops)

00:09:48.839 --> 00:09:50.759
maybe even circulation problems,

00:09:50.759 --> 00:09:53.519
depending on how tight the
neck rings actually are.

00:09:53.519 --> 00:09:56.789
- The idea of stopping
has not crossed my mind

00:09:56.789 --> 00:09:59.999
because it's been in
my mind my whole life.

00:09:59.999 --> 00:10:02.639
Look where she's at and look where I'm at.

00:10:02.639 --> 00:10:05.789
I would love to get my
neck as long as hers.

00:10:05.789 --> 00:10:08.249
- Remember, the way that the ribs move,

00:10:08.249 --> 00:10:10.469
follow a very specific pattern

00:10:10.469 --> 00:10:13.799
to allow maximal expansion of your lungs.

00:10:13.799 --> 00:10:16.169
And when you're limiting rib mobility,

00:10:16.169 --> 00:10:18.119
and changing the rib mobility,

00:10:18.119 --> 00:10:19.889
you're actually decreasing your ability

00:10:19.889 --> 00:10:21.659
to take a full breath.

00:10:21.659 --> 00:10:23.909
And as a result, starting to impact your

00:10:23.909 --> 00:10:25.979
cardiopulmonary performance.
(keyboard clacks)

00:10:25.979 --> 00:10:28.139
- [Sydney] I don't feel very good

00:10:28.139 --> 00:10:30.359
after removing the necklace.

00:10:30.359 --> 00:10:33.629
Wow, it is really bruised.

00:10:33.629 --> 00:10:36.796
It's a little upsetting
to see the bruising.

00:10:36.796 --> 00:10:37.799
(keyboard clacks)
- When you have constant

00:10:37.799 --> 00:10:38.729
pressure on your skin,

00:10:38.729 --> 00:10:41.009
you could actually
cause pressure necrosis.

00:10:41.009 --> 00:10:43.469
This is basically what
happens in a hospital

00:10:43.469 --> 00:10:44.999
when someone stays for
a long period of time

00:10:44.999 --> 00:10:47.969
and is bed-bound, can't walk,
can't rotate in the bed.

00:10:47.969 --> 00:10:49.859
They could actually
develop pressure ulcers.

00:10:49.859 --> 00:10:51.329
They could get so deep to the point

00:10:51.329 --> 00:10:52.919
where the skin gets broken down

00:10:52.919 --> 00:10:53.909
all the way to the bone,

00:10:53.909 --> 00:10:56.336
past even the the adipose or fat tissue.

00:10:56.336 --> 00:10:58.379
(keyboard clacks)
- This is my destiny

00:10:58.379 --> 00:11:02.001
and this is what I've chosen for myself.

00:11:02.001 --> 00:11:02.879
(texts thudding)

00:11:02.879 --> 00:11:04.889
- People take risks all
the time doing things

00:11:04.889 --> 00:11:06.899
that they find valuable and pleasurable.

00:11:06.899 --> 00:11:09.059
And if this culturally
means something to her,

00:11:09.059 --> 00:11:10.529
who are we to judge?
(keyboard clacks)

00:11:10.529 --> 00:11:12.839
- I'm Justin Jedlica, I'm 32 years old,

00:11:12.839 --> 00:11:13.979
and I'm a living doll.

00:11:13.979 --> 00:11:14.909
- A living doll?

00:11:14.909 --> 00:11:16.019
Is that a profession?

00:11:16.019 --> 00:11:17.009
Is that a hobby?
(keyboard clacks)

00:11:17.009 --> 00:11:20.489
- I've had 125 procedures.

00:11:20.489 --> 00:11:22.529
- It's a lot of procedures
(blower whirring)

00:11:22.529 --> 00:11:27.209
- And I spent $158,000 to make
me really resemble a doll.

00:11:27.209 --> 00:11:29.279
- See, I wonder if at any point,

00:11:29.279 --> 00:11:31.769
did his doctors have a discussion

00:11:31.769 --> 00:11:33.629
as to why he wants this?

00:11:33.629 --> 00:11:37.139
Is it healthy to keep going
for surgical procedures?

00:11:37.139 --> 00:11:39.179
Are there other options,
like, getting in shape

00:11:39.179 --> 00:11:40.799
where your muscles can look big

00:11:40.799 --> 00:11:42.179
without having to get implants?

00:11:42.179 --> 00:11:43.049
And I'm only saying that

00:11:43.049 --> 00:11:44.819
because that's a healthier
alternative, not necessarily

00:11:44.819 --> 00:11:45.719
he has to do that.
(keyboard clacks)

00:11:45.719 --> 00:11:47.879
- I started having a couple
other nose revisions.

00:11:47.879 --> 00:11:49.769
Then I'll get a little
fuzzy after a while,

00:11:49.769 --> 00:11:52.109
but at the end, I've
had five nose jobs now.

00:11:52.109 --> 00:11:53.429
- Because I'm not a plastic surgeon,

00:11:53.429 --> 00:11:55.949
I don't know what the qualifications are

00:11:55.949 --> 00:11:58.259
of a person that should
not get plastic surgery.

00:11:58.259 --> 00:12:01.349
But I think if you're getting
multiple facial revisions

00:12:01.349 --> 00:12:04.829
and you're doing it to
replicate an imaginary being,

00:12:04.829 --> 00:12:06.659
I think that's worth an evaluation

00:12:06.659 --> 00:12:07.769
with a mental health specialist,

00:12:07.769 --> 00:12:09.329
at the very least.
(logo whooshing)

00:12:09.329 --> 00:12:11.609
Click here for a clip of
my interview with Steve-O,

00:12:11.609 --> 00:12:13.679
where he shares his biggest regret

00:12:13.679 --> 00:12:15.809
and his most painful injury.

00:12:17.597 --> 00:12:19.976
As always, stay happy and healthy.

00:12:19.976 --> 00:12:23.143
(gentle upbeat music)

